 "description": "An evergreen relative of the oaks that grows in the redwood and mixed evergreen forest, slim and tall under the conifers and round-headed in the open. Its thick, toothed leaves are woolly and buff underneath when young, and it bears big acorns in shaggy cups.",
 "season_notes": {
  "winter": "Leathery leaves hold their olive green in the rain; last fall's acorns lie under the trees.",
  "spring": "New shoots come out felted and pale buff, the crown looks frosted.",
  "summer": "Erect cream catkins stand over the crown with a heavy smell.",
  "fall": "Large acorns in bristly cups fall, after two summers on the tree."
 },
